  <Scene>
    <WorldInfo title="A Bell Curve from Coin Counts" info="&quot;X3D Math Lab • Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.&quot;">
      <MetadataString containerField="metadata" name="mathlab.sample" reference="mathlab.x3d/1" value="&quot;{\&quot;adapter\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.x3d/1\&quot;,\&quot;axes\&quot;:\&quot;Horizontal: standardized count Z. Vertical: density ×6; displayed bar area divided by six equals probability mass.\&quot;,\&quot;bounds\&quot;:{\&quot;center\&quot;:[0.0,1.4925,0.021249999999999998],\&quot;size\&quot;:[11.0,3.515,0.5675]},\&quot;configuration_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;afaec6aba3c6b65e87551a4e09e56de239fb6f8e7128812ea6a0fad872f87436\&quot;,\&quot;insights\&quot;:[\&quot;Mint bar area divided by 6, not bar height, is probability. Both density heights are displayed ×6 for legibility; horizontal standardized coordinates are unchanged.\&quot;,\&quot;The trials are independent and identically distributed Bernoulli(p), with fixed 0&lt;p&lt;1. Their finite, nonzero variance satisfies the classical central limit theorem's assumptions.\&quot;,\&quot;Increasing n changes a distribution computed exactly from the binomial formula. This lesson does not estimate it with random samples or claim that a finite n is already normal.\&quot;,\&quot;The continuous normal assigns zero probability to an individual point, whereas each finite-n count can have positive mass. Compare areas or CDFs, not point probabilities to curve heights.\&quot;],\&quot;lesson\&quot;:\&quot;probability\&quot;,\&quot;metrics\&quot;:[{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;mean\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Standardized mean\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;The exact finite-n reference is zero; this is its floating-point sum.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:2.8760834317430317e-16},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;variance\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Standardized variance\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;The exact finite-n reference is one, before taking any limit.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.0},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;mass\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Total discrete probability\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:1.0},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;normal_error\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Max continuity-corrected CDF gap\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;Measured at k+½ for k=0…n. A finite comparison, not a theorem bound or a density error.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:0.011305830373333992},{\&quot;id\&quot;:\&quot;tail\&quot;,\&quot;label\&quot;:\&quot;Undrawn probability mass\&quot;,\&quot;note\&quot;:\&quot;All outcomes remain in numerical data. Only bars with standardized centers |z|≤4.5 are drawn.\&quot;,\&quot;unit\&quot;:\&quot;\&quot;,\&quot;value\&quot;:3.379220508056638e-06}],\&quot;parameters\&quot;:{\&quot;n\&quot;:12,\&quot;p\&quot;:0.35},\&quot;sample_schema\&quot;:\&quot;mathlab.sample/1\&quot;,\&quot;sample_sha256\&quot;:\&quot;a076a8dc6d9a23dcb601e2e6c8d23dc18f9b3b4edaa68af1dfd6726d78dba083\&quot;,\&quot;scope\&quot;:\&quot;Static sampled geometry and authored lesson parameters; not a proof, live controller, or checkpoint.\&quot;,\&quot;title\&quot;:\&quot;A Bell Curve from Coin Counts\&quot;,\&quot;view\&quot;:\&quot;planar\&quot;}&quot;" />
    </WorldInfo>
